# Tracer: separate candidate clauses provide ordered local formation guards.
# Before (rejected; this behavior is intentionally preserved):
# prop bounded_reciprocal(t R):
#     exist x R st {x != 0 and 1 / x > 0}
# A component's formation check does not assume its assertion inside the and.
#
# Current accepted source: the first whole clause is locally adopted before
# formation of the next clause. Reading observes that existing native order.
prop bounded_reciprocal(t R):
    exist x R st {x != 0, 1 / x > 0}
# This establishes the definition's formation, not a predicate instance or
# existence of a witness. No proof rule or formation policy was changed.
# Boundary: the conjunction version remains an executable negative regression
# in examples/test_statements/negative/def_prop_stmt/compound-formation-order.lit.
# Evidence: target/release/litex -strict -lang en -f examples/stmt_nodes/definition/compound_condition_formation.lit
